title: Route1MoveIn
tags: cutscene
---
<<declare $r1_movein_keys = "">>
<<declare $r1_movein_socks = "">>
<<declare $r1_movein_rules = "">>
// Starts in black: the viewing ends with <<fade_out>> and <<next_scene Route1MoveIn>>.
// She is already waiting on the landing with the keys.
<<place Player PlayerArrive>>
<<place Samantha SamanthaWait>>
<<show Samantha>>
<<face Samantha left>>
<<face Player right>>
<<card "Saturday. Moving day.">>
<<fade_in>>
<<walk Player PlayerKnock>>
<<face Player Samantha>>
<<face Samantha Player>>
{$samantha_name}: Ten o'clock exactly.
{$samantha_name}: Last time you were six minutes early. I was starting to think you'd changed your mind.
You: I got the flat. Why would I change my mind?
{$samantha_name}: People do. Usually right after they read the contract.
<<if $r1_viewing_why == "money">>
    {$samantha_name}: Rent's due on the first. You said it's the one you can afford, so I'm holding you to that.
<<elseif $r1_viewing_why == "light">>
    {$samantha_name}: I told my father what you said about the light. He's been unbearable all week.
<<elseif $r1_viewing_why == "first">>
    {$samantha_name}: You said we were the first to write back. I've decided to take that as a compliment.
<<endif>>
{$samantha_name}: Two keys. The street door and 3B.
{$samantha_name}: Hold out your hand.
-> Okay.
    <<set $r1_movein_keys to "hand">>
    {$samantha_name}: Palm up. Good.
    {$samantha_name}: You do what you're told. That's going to make this very easy.
-> I can just take them.
    <<set $r1_movein_keys to "take">>
    {$samantha_name}: Ah-ah.
    {$samantha_name}: I said hold out your hand.
    You: ...Fine.
    {$samantha_name}: Better.
-> Is there a spare?
    <<set $r1_movein_keys to "spare">>
    {$samantha_name}: There is. I keep it.
    You: Is that normal?
    {$samantha_name}: It's normal here.
// He unlocks his own door for the first time.
<<face Player up>>
<<open_door Door3B>>
<<face Player Samantha>>
{$samantha_name}: One more thing. A housewarming present.
{$samantha_name}: Socks. A matching pair, for once. I couldn't stop thinking about the last ones.
You: They're... pink.
{$samantha_name}: They're blush. And they were on sale in your size. Roughly.
-> Thank you. Really.
    <<set $r1_movein_socks to "thanks">>
    {$samantha_name}: See? Gracious. We'll make a decent tenant of you yet.
-> Aren't these women's socks?
    <<set $r1_movein_socks to "question">>
    {$samantha_name}: They're socks. They don't know who's wearing them.
    {$samantha_name}: Nobody else will either, unless you take your shoes off. Which you will.
-> I'm not wearing these.
    <<set $r1_movein_socks to "refuse">>
    {$samantha_name}: You will. Your floor is cold and you're too proud to buy slippers.
    {$samantha_name}: I'll know if you don't. I'll ask.
{$samantha_name}: Since we're neighbours now. Three rules.
{$samantha_name}: Shoes off inside. Yours too, not just mine.
{$samantha_name}: Music off by eleven. The walls are thin.
{$samantha_name}: And if I knock, you answer.
-> And if I knock?
    <<set $r1_movein_rules to "fair">>
    {$samantha_name}: Then I'll decide whether I'm home.
-> Deal.
    <<set $r1_movein_rules to "deal">>
    {$samantha_name}: That was quick. You didn't even ask what I'd knock for.
-> That's a lot of rules for a neighbour.
    <<set $r1_movein_rules to "pushback">>
    {$samantha_name}: For a neighbour, yes. For the landlord's daughter, it's the bare minimum.
{$samantha_name}: I'll let you settle in.
{$samantha_name}: The bakery opens at six. Bring me a croissant tomorrow. Call it rent.
// She goes back through her own door.
<<walk Samantha SamanthaHome>>
<<hide Samantha>>
<<close_door Door3A>>
// He goes into his flat and the door shuts behind him.
<<walk Player PlayerInto3B>>
<<face Player down>>
<<close_door Door3B>>
<<wait 1>>
{$samantha_name}: Shoes!
You: ...They're off.
// Time skip to the next morning. He is back up the stairs from the bakery. When this
// node ends the player walks freely; knocking on 3A starts Route1Croissant (door_3a.yarn).
<<fade_out>>
<<place Player PlayerArrive>>
<<face Player right>>
<<card "Sunday morning.">>
<<fade_in>>
You: Six o'clock. One croissant. Her door.
===
